      "title": "First-Order ODEs: Separation of Variables",
      "kind": "prose",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A separable differential equation can be rearranged so that all terms involving the dependent variable are on one side and all terms involving the independent variable are on the other. This method allows you to integrate both sides separately to find the solution."
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Recognize the separable form: If dy/dx = f(x)g(y), the equation is separable.",
        "Rearrange the equation: Move all y terms to one side and all x terms to the other: dy/g(y) = f(x) dx.",
        "Integrate both sides: Perform the integration on each side separately.",
